  "question": "You are a graph image parsing assistant.\n\nThe images show partial views of a related directed capacity network. Same E* labels indicate the same node across views, and the number displayed on each edge is its capacity.\n\nInspect all graph images and reconstruct every graph shown. Do not infer relation meanings or facts that are not visible in the images.\n\nReturn exactly one JSON object with this schema:\n{\n  \"graphs\": [\n    {\n      \"graph_id\": \"G1\",\n      \"triples\": [\n        [\"E18\", 5, \"E19\"],\n        [\"E80\", \"\", \"\"]\n      ]\n    }\n  ]\n}\n\nRules:\n- Preserve every graph ID and keep graph boundaries separate.\n- Extract every node. A node with no incident edge must be emitted as [\"<node label>\", \"\", \"\"]. Replace <node label> with the actual label.\n- Extract every edge as [\"src\", <capacity>, \"dst\"] with a positive integer capacity, and emit each edge once.\n- All graphs are directed; preserve each arrow direction and do not infer a reverse edge.\n- Preserve node labels and capacity numbers exactly. The relation labels are not displayed on capacity edges; do not invent them.\n- Do not include nodes, directed fields, explanations, Markdown, or any additional keys.",
